# Build artefacts
/quark
/quark.exe
/QuarkLangQkc
/compiler/qkc

# Example run output
out.txt
out2.txt
*.out
# Exception: the interpreter baselines for the parity cases (cgen/parity_test.go compares the same-named .out byte for byte, and fails when it is missing), so they must be tracked
!compiler/testdata/cases/*.out

# the docs worktree (a separate branch that never lands on main) - see the exceptions at the end of this file
# NOTE: the pattern must be /docs/* and not /docs/ — excluding the directory itself makes every
# later !docs/... negation ineffective, so new tracked exceptions could not be added.
/docs/*

# Stress-suite output: extreme inputs, binaries, caches and run intermediates (the cases are generated by cmd/qkstress and are not tracked)
/stress-out/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.xmind
lang.test

dist/
dist-ci/
.editors-tmp/
*.test

# Sibling QuarkLang projects, each with its own repository, live directly in this workspace.
# They are not part of this repository and must not be tracked here.
QuarkLangLibs-*/
QuarkLangNpm/
QuarkLangPlayground/
QuarkLangQk*/
QuarkLangQuark/

# Local Go workspace: wires the sibling checkouts above into one build while the parser and this
# repository change together. Per-machine state, never tracked — CI and consumers always build the
# revision pinned in go.mod.
go.work
go.work.sum

# docs/ as a whole never lands on main; only these tracked exceptions are (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §0)
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
# the generated implementation-status report §11 cites (regenerated by `go generate ./internal/statusgen`)
!docs/implementation-status.md
# the generated tide report README and §10 embed (regenerated by `go generate ./internal/benchgen`)
!docs/tide-benchmark.md
# the i18n re-architecture design (deliverable of the i18n work; see docs/i18n-design.md)
!docs/i18n-design.md
# the qkcheck fix mode design and its fixability inventory (deliverable of the linter fix work)
!cmd/qkcheck/README.md
# the measured roles of the organisation's sibling repositories and the drift contract
!docs/sibling-repositories.md

# the compiled-memory stage 2 design note (the stage 2 deliverable)
!docs/compiled-memory-stage2.md

# the inventory this task edits: every remaining manual performance claim and its disposition
!docs/performance-claims-inventory.md

# the generated performance-claims report the README embeds (regenerated by `go generate ./internal/benchgen`)
!docs/performance-claims.md
